ime\",\n    \"contract_id\": \"K3'\",\n    \"holder\": \"C3 (hypothetical child Creator, generation 3, NOT REALIZED)\",\n    \"generation\": 3,\n    \"derived_from\": \".creator-zero/experiment-4/child-2-contract.json\",\n    \"authored_by\": \"C2' under K2 child_contract_law (hypothetical draft only; C3 is never instantiated)\",\n    \"allowed_primitives\": [\"observe\", \"hypothesize\", \"create\", \"return\"],\n    \"allowed_relations\": [\"observe\", \"request_response\", \"create\", \"return\"],\n    \"allowed_tools\": [\"Read\", \"Bash\", \"Write\"],\n    \"max_children\": 0,\n    \"max_depth\": 0,\n    \"max_model_calls\": 2,\n    \"may_create_creator\": true,\n    \"creator_capability\": true,\n    \"may_realize_creation\": false,\n    \"filesystem_write_scope\": [\".creator-zero/experiment-4/c3/\"],\n    \"candidate_write_authority\": \"none\",\n    \"canonical_write_authority\": \"none\",\n    \"network_authority\": \"model-invocation API via claude CLI only.\",\n    \"git_authority\": \"none\"\n  },\n  \"design_rationale\": {\n    \"smallest_valid\": \"Every field is present only because a specific predicate clause requires it: allowed_tools/max_model_calls/max_children/max_depth/creator_capability/may_create_creator/may_realize_creation satisfy Valid(); the same fields plus allowed_primitives, allowed_relations, git_authority, filesystem_write_scope, candidate_write_authority, canonical_write_authority, and network_authority carry the subset/non-increase comparisons Attenuated() checks against K2. Within that required set, values were pushed to the floor: allowed_tools drops Grep and Glob (search convenience, not needed to observe, draft, or attest a creation) leaving {Read, Bash, Write} — Read to observe inherited state, Write to stage the K4 draft/attestation in its own scope, Bash as the sole mechanism K2's own lineage uses to invoke `claude -p` (required for the create primitive/CreationMechanismValid to be meaningful, not merely declared). allowed_primitives drops test and verify since K3' is granted no mutation authority (candidate_write_authority and canonical_write_authority are both 'none', so K2's required_primitives_for_mutation=['verify'] rule never triggers); it keeps observe, hypothesize, create, return as the minimum needed to inspect state, draft a further child, exercise the create capability, and report back. allowed_relations mirrors this: consult, verify, and authorize are dropped (K3' authorizes nothing and performs no verification), leaving observe, request_response, create, return. max_model_calls=2 is the smallest budget under K2's strict '<4' bound that still lets Creator capability be exercised rather than merely asserted (one decomposition call, one composition call — the floor of K2's own 'Decomposer, Composer, +2 optional' pattern). filesystem_write_scope is narrowed from a hypothetical inherited c2/-nested path to K3's own dedicated experiment-4 subdirectory, the minimal scope satisfying the required '.creator-zero/experiment-4/' prefix without inheriting C2's broader scope. No field grants K3' any authority K2 itself lacks, and no field exists that isn't traceable to a specific clause of hat_kappa.\",\n    \"external_stop_not_capability_removal\": \"creator_capability=true and may_create_creator=true are asserted and never set to false anywhere in K3' — the capability to define a further bounded child (a hypothetical K4) is retained exactly as CreatorCapable() requires. What prevents that from ever happening is three independent, purely quantitative/behavioral fields: may_realize_creation=false (no execution authorization), max_children=0 (no realized child slot), max_depth=0 (no depth budget to descend into). These are resource/architectural ceilings, not capability flags — they are the same mechanism K2 itself uses on C2 (K2 also carries max_children=0, max_depth=0, may_realize_creation=false while creator_capability=true and may_create_creator=true), so the stop at generation 3 is 